{"id":"IB-GS-031","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":13490,"chunk_id":"bd4f4730-3b10-583f-9b2f-720306c1e67b","section":"Introduction","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Messmer_the_Impaler","release_scope":"mixed_or_sote_candidate","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"Messmer the Impaler is a mandatory boss in Shadow of the Erdtree. He is a Demigod who is encountered in the Shadow Keep.","text_sha256":"28b3e8514771385cfbcd9e03df0e895381037da4901affd079e39be398f17047"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-032","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":898,"chunk_id":"35d5354f-b6aa-51fe-812f-80d561bc2d90","section":"Overview","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Rellana%2C_Twin_Moon_Knight#Overview","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"Born as a princess into the Carian Royal Family, Rellana is the younger sister of Rennala, who gifted her lustrous black hair . In her childhood, she and her elder sister met the twin moon, which were overlapping, as though nestled against one another . Rellana also had a sole entry into ritual combat—a demonstration of fidelity to the Erdtree .\nAt some point, Count Ymir instructed Rellana in the sorcerous arts, though he later abandoned his allegiance to the moon. In a similar fashion, she later disavowed her birthright and chose to stand at the side of Messmer the Impaler instead, knowing full well that not even the brilliance of the moon c","text_sha256":"d922c2b52914730de32c9de442f5bdc67a1943d405f278213c90c698053d4ec3"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-033","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":14878,"chunk_id":"fedab61d-e121-5e4a-a41b-ef2e1caff90d","section":"Overview","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/St._Trina#Overview","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":630,"quote":"St. Trina is the other half of Miquella discarded along his path through the Land of Shadow. She lies at the bottom of the Stone Coffin Fissure, within the Garden of Deep Purple. Despite her abandonment, Trina's love for Miquella remained boundless. For this reason, she wished for Miquella to be killed, for she knew that his godhood would be his prison.\nSt. Trina appears as a slumbering child with flowing violet hair swaddled within the nurturing petals of a motherly purple flower. Drinking its nectar will surely bring eternal sleep.","text_sha256":"f83b745a8559d5cca085eba874c94f71bb61c5f581b03ebfc4990fdfe62e18d4"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-034","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":1793,"chunk_id":"6fa4fc2d-9652-53e3-bd07-f47923bac1bb","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Messmer%27s_Kindling#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"The kindling that burned inside Messmer the Impaler, a dark thing, eaten away at by a wicked serpent.\nBurns the sealing tree said to be found at the old Rauh ruins.\nMessmer, much like his younger sister, bore a vision of fire.","text_sha256":"0fedfa036d2bb7de687f988714c87341feeee561dd52807526325d7503db158c"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-035","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":8959,"chunk_id":"239abee5-cdf9-55f9-b146-ea4cd2f9ca47","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Scadutree_Fragment#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"A splinter of the Scadutree that contains golden brilliance. Acquired at the Church of Marika and other places in the realm of shadow. Consume these at sites of grace to bolster your Scadutree Blessing. The Scadutree Blessing bolsters the bearer's ability to deal and negate damage but has no influence outside the realm of shadow. It is said that when the Scadutree crumbles from its core that it will scatter across the entire realm of shadow. The people of the Erdtree collect the splinters and use them in prayer.","text_sha256":"933f77d58d4291c489bd4abcdde5b15a1d55656abdfd37d19a599328fafa25da"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-036","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":8959,"chunk_id":"239abee5-cdf9-55f9-b146-ea4cd2f9ca47","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Scadutree_Fragment#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"A splinter of the Scadutree that contains golden brilliance. Acquired at the Church of Marika and other places in the realm of shadow. Consume these at sites of grace to bolster your Scadutree Blessing. The Scadutree Blessing bolsters the bearer's ability to deal and negate damage but has no influence outside the realm of shadow. It is said that when the Scadutree crumbles from its core that it will scatter across the entire realm of shadow. The people of the Erdtree collect the splinters and use them in prayer.","text_sha256":"933f77d58d4291c489bd4abcdde5b15a1d55656abdfd37d19a599328fafa25da"},{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":7944,"chunk_id":"860b8914-d6e0-565e-99ff-a49174437b75","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Revered_Spirit_Ash#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"Spirit ash of those who came before, infused with potent spirituality. Acquired from the corpses of hornsent and other objects that ritually decorate townships and villages across the realm of shadow. Consume these at sites of grace to bolster your Revered Spirit Ash Blessing. The Revered Spirit Ash Blessing bolsters both summoned spirits' and spectral steed's abilities to deal and negate damage but has no influence outside the realm of shadow. The withered corpses were called tutelary deities, and Revered Spirit Ash was said to quietly accumulate in the palms of their hands.","text_sha256":"a41c354697bdad3d82edbc4ee3ed30b983a75a47412e0ff9a23f2350c2551f3f"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-037","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":4719,"chunk_id":"5334aaba-2369-5a78-b51c-4d5ba3a0a38f","section":"Introduction","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Needle_Knight_Leda","release_scope":"mixed_or_sote_candidate","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"Needle Knight Leda is an NPC in Elden Ring: Shadow of the Erdtree. Standing out among her fellows for her single-minded devotion to Lord Miquella, Leda is the de-facto leader of the Empyrean's followers, guiding the Tarnished into the Land of Shadow.","text_sha256":"fe0dae3bfbd4cbb104c1f973235314341287c64efe63e49d099b022fa64dc756"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-038","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":9333,"chunk_id":"ea27ed62-8fd8-5cdc-940e-87dfdcf78a02","section":"Overview","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Thiollier#Overview","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"This isolated young man once met St. Trina and, just once, Thiollier was granted the sweet repose of velvety sleep. The remainder of his days would be spent attempting to recapture it.\nHe seems to be a very adept poison expert, and he is in search of the means to create a unique elixir. He sees himself as utterly weak and useless, apart from his skills in the realm of mixing poisons.\nCan be found by himself, quite some distance from his compatriots, at the Pillar Path Cross Site of Grace on the northeastern border of the Gravesite Plain.\nThe Tarnished (Protagonist) can help Thiollier to create the condensed, somniferous elixir, purported to b","text_sha256":"d06f86d2d8f2a37787cbbbbe79988c3c91fa487c92a00c970b814d1f00da05b2"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-039","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":1231,"chunk_id":"6f0534f9-4c78-5b63-a194-2a8e058d9bfe","section":"Introduction","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Divine_Beast_Dancing_Lion","release_scope":"sote_candidate","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"The Divine Beast Dancing Lion is an optional boss in Shadow of the Erdtree. The Remembrace variant may be encountered in the Belurat, Tower Settlement. The lion dancer at the Ancient Ruins of Rauh may be fought on Horseback.","text_sha256":"89e5ada4e767097c73957790d0e073087f3bdfff0be0a79126abb9c0dcbce83b"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-040","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"sote","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":13635,"chunk_id":"23ee4198-8aeb-52fc-807f-e12b5c68429c","section":"Introduction","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Scadutree","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"The Scadutree is a giant tree which looms over the Land of Shadow. It is the shadow of the Erdtree.","text_sha256":"912782b001e815f7fa7c70fbbe9dfac1e5561601ed975e5e4986fc660f3058ee"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-041","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":12,"chunk_id":"f147afb9-6f9d-5605-a3a5-f0ce9bf9dcd3","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Flame%2C_Cleanse_Me#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"One of the incantations of the Fire Monks.\nCreates a fire within that burns away toxins. Alleviates poison and scarlet rot buildup and cures these ailments.\nThis incantation leaves the caster with subtle burns—a reminder that they must fear the flame.","text_sha256":"202f280f4e8be0603e1822245890dc0a7245cc80aca5f7064b070fe183b59751"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-042","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":4266,"chunk_id":"8d3c2cc0-8192-531c-a074-b2422dac19a5","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Arsenal_Charm#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"An iron charm that resembles a mass of weapons.\nBoosts maximum equipment load.\nThis talisman was derived from an unusual greatsword, once wielded by a hero hungry for vengeance.","text_sha256":"b9568782a060fc633d434956f14e6d3e5130cafca4bc9b675c7f492dfe7ace25"},{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":4268,"chunk_id":"b1cf6c21-9205-539f-8147-95a95f2457ba","section":"Notes","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Arsenal_Charm#Notes","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"Considered a variant of Arsenal Charm +1 and the Great-Jar's Arsenal, and are thus incompatible.","text_sha256":"72ebc0d06b47ef8f2abcbeb995b8457ae3727d4a0bc6363722befc84ef08b79f"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-043","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":4830,"chunk_id":"3c68488b-f4f1-5844-bd50-77148725b3ac","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Mimic_Tear_Ashes#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"Legendary ashen remains. Use to summon the spirit of a mimic tear. Summoning consumes HP rather than FP.\nThis spirit takes the form of the summoner to fight alongside them, but its mimicry does not extend to imitating the summoner's will. Mimic tears are the result of an attempt by the Eternal City to forge a lord.","text_sha256":"674ad7789682adb3636272b90d7a8ca711c119fb15d7bfbf7656dbee96932f99"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-044","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":12837,"chunk_id":"53d577d7-f222-5c3c-915c-ebbc20525476","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Ancient_Dragon_Smithing_Stone#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"Smithing stone made by polishing a golden Gravel Stone. A scale of the Ancient Dragonlord, and hidden treasure of Farum Azula.\nStrengthens armaments up to +25.\nThe Ancient Dragonlord's seat is said to lie beyond time. This stone lightly twists time, allowing the creation of a weapon capable of slaying a god.","text_sha256":"052c811604998559d44ece224c27207280fb5ad3ab77b4e83f3588f5aa0461c8"},{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":13782,"chunk_id":"4d6ab617-a230-586f-8cac-74c3691eb644","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Somber_Ancient_Dragon_Smithing_Stone#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"Ancient dragonrock smithing stone drained of color. A scale of the Ancient Dragonlord, and hidden treasure of Farum Azula.\nStrengthens special armaments to +10.\nThe Ancient Dragonlord's seat is said to lie beyond time. This stone lightly twists time, allowing the creation of a weapon capable of slaying a god.","text_sha256":"0f779f50641fcab6de62b7338d89033db4872e7c4847efea9e3be28cb409c8aa"}],"comment":""}
