{"id":"IB-GS-046","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":7,"chunk_id":"6b0c3670-3d9a-5f45-be0f-0691d054c60e","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Ash_of_War%3A_Golden_Vow#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"This Ash of War grants an armament the Sacred affinity and the following skill:\n\"Golden Vow: Skill passed down from antiquity among the knights of the capital. Raise armament aloft and pledge to honor the Erdtree in battle, granting self and nearby allies increased attack power and defense.\"\nUsable on all melee armaments.","text_sha256":"3c28071a06b758bef598445b26e3851a5e84145b338950b04ece6f519de27009"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-047","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":13465,"chunk_id":"a92bd10a-2192-5ce4-9bce-c51add6f875f","section":"Notes","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Bloodhound%27s_Fang#Notes","release_scope":"base_candidate","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":307,"quote":"Bloodhound's Fang is one of only two Somber Smithing Stone-based weapons that can receive Weapon Buffs.\nBloodflame Blade is generally the strongest option for this, as the combination of extra Fire Attack Power and additional Blood Loss build-up is quite good for a fairly small investment in Faith and Arcane required to cast it.\nAs implied in the description, the jump attacks of Bloodhound's Fang deal much more damage when compared to the jump attacks of the same weapon class. This is due to the jump attacks of the Bloodhound's Fang having higher motion values than usual.\nThe motion values for all four jump attacks on the Bloodhound's Fang ar","text_sha256":"768bd373ecccbdd223e49b617cd4b9996129069150b3b56f2203ebf1584b1f2e"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-048","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":13,"chunk_id":"eb3ea611-5a79-5c45-a54e-abd5b16739da","section":"Notes","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Flame%2C_Cleanse_Me#Notes","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"Costs 14 FP per cast.\nCosts 10 Stamina per cast.\nRequires 1 Memory Slot.\nThe reason that Frostbite is only removed when fully applied instead of also when it's building up is because the flat HP damage is considered to be Fire damage, and an effect of that damage type is that it removes applied Frostbite.","text_sha256":"712871848dd2d4924ef1f611f35b1a84a82c5ad57a7504550a846c93e26da8c9"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-049","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":528,"chunk_id":"a6b4ee17-d60a-5e24-8c2e-9704a0cc1b29","section":"Questline Progression","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Ranni_the_Witch#Questline_Progression","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"Completing Ranni's questline will unlock the Age of the Stars ending.\n(Optional) Church of Elleh\nAfter meeting Melina and obtaining the Spectral Steed Whistle, use Torrent at least once. After that, rest on any Site of Grace. Then, fast travel to the Church of Elleh Site of Grace and find Ranni (using the pseudonym \"Renna\") sitting on a broken wall. Exhaust her dialogue to receive the Spirit Calling Bell and Lone Wolf Ashes.\nIf you miss this step, these items will be available for purchase at the Twin Maiden Husks in Roundtable Hold -- 200 runes for the Lone Wolf Ashes and 1,000 runes for the Spirit Calling Bell respectively.\nRanni's Rise\nRanni can next be encountered on the top floor of Ranni's Rise, accessible by clearing Caria Manor. This stage varies depending on whether you have defeated her brother, Starscourge Radahn, or given Sorcerer Rogier the Black Knifeprint.\nAgree to become one of Ranni's vassals, and then head back down th","text_sha256":"1b797503851ee134fc7082bf3d8af0d62511ff8fb8d9dbb6ee4b1c383852abe9"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-050","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":529,"chunk_id":"aecc4330-52c2-5cae-a933-3189b64a2c5e","section":"Questline Progression","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Ranni_the_Witch#Questline_Progression","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":0,"quote":"Bring the Fingerslayer Blade to Ranni, who will give you the Carian Inverted Statue. This key item is required for Fia's questline, however it is not necessary to complete Ranni's questline.\nWARNING: This will immediately end Preceptor Seluvis's quest.\nAinsel River\nRenna's Rise will now be open after giving Ranni the Fingerslayer Blade. Enter and climb to the top, and go through the sending gate to the upper portion of Ainsel River.\nPick up the Miniature Ranni near the spawn point and rest at the Ainsel River Main Site of Grace. Use the \"Talk to miniature Ranni\" option three times to get her to speak.\n(Optional) Ranni will also have dialogue ","text_sha256":"66e37927cdd73fdfd0b3ae57f1ec69b303f838c696f2be18fecb73ced50d80c5"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-051","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":529,"chunk_id":"aecc4330-52c2-5cae-a933-3189b64a2c5e","section":"Questline Progression","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Ranni_the_Witch#Questline_Progression","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":437,"quote":"Pick up the Miniature Ranni near the spawn point and rest at the Ainsel River Main Site of Grace. Use the \"Talk to miniature Ranni\" option three times to get her to speak.\n(Optional) Ranni will also have dialogue at the Nokstella, Eternal City and Nokstella Waterfall Basin Sites of Grace. These are not required to continue her questline.\nDefeat the Baleful Shadow invader just past the Nokstella Waterfall Basin Site of Grace to obtain the Discarded Palace Key. Go to Rennala's boss room in Academy of Raya Lucaria and unlock the chest to obtain the Dark Moon Ring.\nMoonlight Altar\nDefeat Astel, Naturalborn of the Void at the end of the Lake of Ro","text_sha256":"66e37927cdd73fdfd0b3ae57f1ec69b303f838c696f2be18fecb73ced50d80c5"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-052","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":529,"chunk_id":"aecc4330-52c2-5cae-a933-3189b64a2c5e","section":"Questline Progression","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Ranni_the_Witch#Questline_Progression","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":777,"quote":"Defeat the Baleful Shadow invader just past the Nokstella Waterfall Basin Site of Grace to obtain the Discarded Palace Key. Go to Rennala's boss room in Academy of Raya Lucaria and unlock the chest to obtain the Dark Moon Ring.\nMoonlight Altar\nDefeat Astel, Naturalborn of the Void at the end of the Lake of Rot and travel up the lift. This lift only unlocks if you have obtained the Dark Moon Ring.\nTravel to the Cathedral of Manus Celes and descend through the tunnel near the altar to find Ranni sitting on the corpse of her Two Fingers. Interact with her to trigger a cutscene. After the cutscene, speak to her again and she will disappear, leavi","text_sha256":"66e37927cdd73fdfd0b3ae57f1ec69b303f838c696f2be18fecb73ced50d80c5"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-053","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":3180,"chunk_id":"15c9ae39-5127-5a57-980b-e048a52d38cb","section":"Notes","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Malenia%2C_Blade_of_Miquella#Notes","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"wiki_prose","quote_start":597,"quote":"Once defeated, she will leave behind a large, solid Scarlet Aeonia in her arena. If the player has the Unalloyed Gold Needle after completing Millicent's questline, it can be given to the Aeonia to receive Miquella's Needle and an Somber Ancient Dragon Smithing Stone\nMillicent and her four sisters are implied to be descended from Malenia in some way, but more as offshoots, or buds, of her Scarlet Bloom rather than actual daughters. They are also referred to as Scarlet Valkyries.","text_sha256":"f5a0ed7c81de30d5ad8e5ba81f7cd2197dc1d4372c860466d1b50ec458cf3e1b"}],"comment":""}
{"id":"IB-GS-054","assigned_to":"TV2 - UncleThing","status":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"checks":{"source_urls":"pending","expected_answer":"pending","difficulty":"pending","scope":"pending"},"evaluation_scope":"elden_ring","author_basis":"local_snapshot","author_evidence":[{"artifact":"backend/data/chunk_runs/s2-full-v1/chunks.jsonl","line":2693,"chunk_id":"8271647d-7aa8-599f-8d39-7a46841c6b78","section":"Description","source_url":"https://eldenring.wiki.gg/wiki/Radagon%27s_Soreseal#%F0%9F%8F%B4%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%A2%F3%A0%81%A5%F3%A0%81%AE%F3%A0%81%A7%F3%A0%81%BF-0","release_scope":"unknown","source_type":"in_game_text","quote_start":0,"quote":"This legendary talisman is an eye engraved with an Elden Rune, said to be the seal of King Consort Radagon.\nGreatly raises vigor, endurance, strength, dexterity, but also increases damage taken by a similar measure.\nSolemn duty weighs upon the one beholden; not unlike a gnawing curse from which there is no deliverance.","text_sha256":"88abe497c15680a58fdbb053a2566ffd3491af334235919d527685afaf247fb4"}],"comment":""}
